<p>Cape Verdean health authorities denied the MV Hondius permission to dock at Praia after three passengers died and officials identified seven confirmed or suspected hantavirus cases on the polar expedition cruise ship, according to the World Health Organization and local authorities. The vessel, operated by Netherlands-based Oceanwide Expeditions, remained off Cape Verde as health officials coordinated medical evacuations and assessed whether it could continue toward Spain’s Canary Islands. WHO said laboratory testing had confirmed at least one case early in the investigation; later accounts cited two lab-verified infections and additional suspected cases under review. The ship left southern Argentina in March with 149 people from 23 countries, and health authorities were investigating how a rodent-borne virus associated with severe respiratory illness reached the vessel.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Fey1Mzhlz_vh7ogJR_F2xwTxRHKaF3dwWEntgqbWqdfY0GUU0UFTmitQw6gPjmwbh-EXjjo_LQZ8Eh9Z7JU_oALqCHFcoOn5lhJUg8rQu6dRC7cEs5Ne0eQeOYxj6jG8ig12D4ra35e9OdyN_deekePMu8qJ5he75Ry6vSVTn8IhNTPXXcv_ci0bIPBxlQ3HuB_CLqcrG3y-IO04jenlZg' alt='The cruise ship MV Hondius stationed off the port of Praia, Cape Verde, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Victims identified: The operator identified the dead passengers as a Dutch couple and a German national.</li><li>Urgent cases: A British crew member needed urgent medical care, and a UK passenger remained in critical but stable condition after being hospitalized.</li><li>Previous stops: The reported itinerary included Antarctic and other stops before the vessel reached the Cape Verde area.</li><li>Public risk: WHO assessed the risk to the broader public as low and said travel restrictions were not required.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>World Health Organization: WHO said passengers and crew were receiving medical care and support, and virus sequencing was ongoing. (<a href='https://europeansting.com/2026/05/04/three-dead-in-suspected-hantavirus-infection-outbreak-on-cruise-ship-who/'>The European Sting</a>)</li><li>Oceanwide Expeditions: The Dutch operator said strict precautionary measures were in place on board, including isolation, hygiene protocols and medical monitoring. (<a href='https://www.fastcompany.com/91536116/hantavirus-cruise-ship-outbreak-deadly-health-incident-update'>Fast Company</a>)</li><li>Cape Verde health authorities: They handled port-health clearance at Praia while the outbreak assessment remained unresolved. (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/05/cape-verde-denies-docking-to-hantavirus-hit-cruise-ship-as-who-confirms-seven-cases'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>South Africa health department: Spokesman Foster Mohale told The New York Times the public need not panic because only two patients from the cruise ship had been within South Africa. (<a href='https://www.fastcompany.com/91536116/hantavirus-cruise-ship-outbreak-deadly-health-incident-update'>Fast Company</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cruise-ship-waiting-after-suspected-outbreak-rare-hantavirus-132630269'>Cruise ship waiting for help after suspected outbreak of hantavirus onboard killed 3</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/environment/article/2026/05/05/how-a-dream-cruise-turned-into-a-health-nightmare_6753127_114.html'>How a dream cruise turned into a health nightmare</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/05/cape-verde-denies-docking-to-hantavirus-hit-cruise-ship-as-who-confirms-seven-cases'>Cape Verde denies docking to hantavirus-hit cruise ship as WHO confirms seven cases</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/04/world/hantavirus-cruise-ship-outbreak-hondius.html'>What to Know About the Suspected Hantavirus Outbreak on an Atlantic Cruise Ship</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/may/04/cruise-ship-suspected